title: '[pallet-revive] Charge the minimum modexp gas cost when the modulus length is zero'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/12691

    The modexp precompile returned an empty output for `mod_len == 0` before charging any
    weight, so those calls were free and skipped the EIP-2565 floor of 200 gas. It now charges
    `MIN_GAS_COST` before that early return. The `base_len == 0 && mod_len == 0` branch, which
    the early return made unreachable, is removed.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
